      "html": "<ul><li>A flood survey has three parts: exposure, resilience and escape of water.</li><li>Flood zones and Flood Re set the scene. The survey shows what the maps cannot.</li><li>Flood resilience means barriers, valves, raised services and tough materials.</li><li>Escape of water is a common home insurance loss. Put it in the report.</li><li>A photo taken on the spot beats a note typed later.</li><li>Quickler writes the report. It does not price risk or model flood depth.</li></ul>"
